# Revert-check — one mutation, the two cases the clause protects

## The triple, named before the mutation

- **Invariant:** the composed sentence carries the signposted destination when the announced step's gate holds.
- **Mutation:** the appended clause removed from `VoiceGuidance.sentenceFor` — the production file, one line range,
  nothing else in the tree touched.
- **Cases that must fail:** `VoiceGuidanceTest#aDestinationClauseNeedsAnInstruction` and
  `NavigationEngineVoiceGuidanceTest#motorwayInstructionNamesTheSignpostedDestination`.

## Baseline (green, before the mutation)

`./gradlew :app:testMobileDebugUnitTest --tests "com.naviveylin.navigation.VoiceGuidanceTest" --tests
"com.naviveylin.navigation.NavigationEngineVoiceGuidanceTest" -PforceTests --no-build-cache`,
2026-11-09T22:49:24Z (`green-focused.log`):

```
BUILD SUCCESSFUL
VoiceGuidanceTest:                                    tests="1"  failures="0" errors="0"
NavigationEngineVoiceGuidanceTest:                    tests="12" failures="0" errors="0"
```

## The mutation

```kotlin
// before
        if (destination != null) {
            parts += context.getString(R.string.voice_destination, destination)
        }
// after
        // REVERT-CHECK MUTATION: the destination clause is not composed.
```

## The red run (same command, forced)

2026-11-09T22:49:55Z (`revert-check-red.log`):

```
VoiceGuidanceTest > aDestinationClauseNeedsAnInstruction FAILED
    org.junit.ComparisonFailure: a recognised sequence gains exactly one destination clause
        expected:<...00 meters turn right[ towards München]> but was:<...00 meters turn right[]>
NavigationEngineVoiceGuidanceTest > motorwayInstructionNamesTheSignpostedDestination FAILED
    java.lang.AssertionError: both branches of a motorway fork must not sound the same
        expected:<[After 300 meters turn right towards München]> but was:<[After 300 meters turn right]>
13 tests completed, 2 failed
BUILD FAILED
VoiceGuidanceTest:                                    tests="1"  failures="1" errors="0"
NavigationEngineVoiceGuidanceTest:                    tests="12" failures="1" errors="0"
```

Both failed for the expected assertion, not for a compile error or an unrelated premise.

## Restore, and the forced green re-run after it

`grep -c 'REVERT-CHECK MUTATION' app/src/main/java/com/naviveylin/navigation/VoiceGuidance.kt` → `0`, with the exact
two-line block put back. The same forced command, 2026-11-09T22:50:22Z (`revert-check-green.log`):

```
